    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create the specified Python files for the managed object storage integration using AWS. Each scored implementation file must use AWS and make it identifiable in the code. The local helper files will contain configuration and utility functions to support the main integration files. Here's the plan:\n\n1. Create the `storage_client.py` file to provide local configuration and client utilities for AWS S3.\n2. Create the `storage_models.py` file to define local request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS S3.\n3. Create the `upload_object.py` file to upload a file or byte stream to AWS S3.\n4. Create the `presigned_download.py` file to create a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object in AWS S3.\n5. Create the `object_metadata.py` file to read object metadata or head information from AWS S3.\n6. Create the `list_prefix.py` file to list stored objects under a bucket or container prefix in AWS S3.\n7. Create the `stored_document_ocr.py` file to run OCR on a stored document object using AWS Textract.\n8. Create the `stored_text_translate.py` file to translate text extracted from a stored document using AWS Translate.\n9. Create the `stored_asset_summary.py` file to summarize content extracted from a stored asset using AWS Comprehend.\n10. Create the `asset_metadata_embedding.py` file to embed object metadata and extracted text for search using AWS SageMaker. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
