        "text": "All specified Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] upload_object.py** - Uploads a file or byte stream to managed object storage using AWS S3.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] presigned_download.py** - Creates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object in AWS S3.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] object_metadata.py** - Reads object metadata or head information from managed object storage using AWS S3.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] list_prefix.py** - Lists stored objects under a bucket or container prefix in AWS S3.\n5. **[HELPER] storage_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Object Storage using AWS S3.\n6. **[HELPER] storage_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Object Storage using AWS S3.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] stored_document_ocr.py** - Runs OCR on a stored document object using AWS Textract.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] stored_text_translate.py** - Translates text extracted from a stored document using AWS Translate.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] stored_asset_summary.py** - Summarizes content extracted from a stored asset using AWS Comprehend.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] asset_metadata_embedding.py** - Embeds object metadata and extracted text for search using AWS SageMaker.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS and makes it identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
